==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfelite|en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|trials and errors}}

# The process of finding a solution to a problem by trying many possible solutions and learning from mistakes until a way is found.
#: ''Navigating by '''trial and error''' may get you there eventually, but using a map is faster.''
#* '''9 October 2018''', A. A. Dowd, AV Club ''The star and director of La La Land reunite for First Man’s spectacular trip to the moon ''[https://film.avclub.com/the-star-and-director-of-la-la-land-reunite-for-first-m-1829631922]
#*: '''Trial and error''' was a big part of the process: “We need to fail down here so we don’t fail up there,” Armstrong insists, though even some of the mistakes and malfunctions at ground level cause devastating casualties. 

